1. When Only One GL Category is Returned 

a. Newly Added GL Category (No Historical Data) 

If the GL Category is newly introduced and there is no historical transaction reference: 

The system will use this GL Category as the prediction result. No further LLM callout is required. 

A low confidence score will be assigned, indicating that the prediction should be reviewed manually if needed. 

Base score 

b. Old GL Category (No Historical Data) 

If the GL Category already exists but has no past transaction history, then: 

The system will use this GL Category as the prediction result. No further LLM callout is required. 

A low confidence score will be assigned, indicating that the prediction should be reviewed manually if needed. 

Base score 

c. Old GL Category (Historical Data available) 

If the GL Category already exists but has past transaction history, then: 

The system will directly use the GL Category that has history. 

No further LLM validation is needed. 

0.5*Si(max)+0.2F+0.3R(most recent) 

 

2. When Multiple GL Categories are Returned 

a. All GL Categories Are Without History 

If none of the returned GL Categories have any past reference: 

The system cannot select a confident match. 

The output is “No GL Code Found.” 

0 

b. Only One GL Category Has Historical Reference, Others are without historical reference  

If multiple GL Categories are returned, but only one of them has past records (and others are old but unused): 

The system will directly use the GL Category that has history. 

No further LLM validation is needed. 

0.5*Si(max)+0.2F+0.3R(most recent) 

 

c. Only One GL Category Has Historical Reference, Others Are Newly added (No History) 

If one category has history, and one or more others are newly added with no history: 

The system will use this GL Category as the prediction result. No further LLM callout is required. 

The confidence score will be low, since new GL Categories might become valid in future. 

Base score 

d. Some GL Categories Have History, and at Least One New Category Exists (No History) 

If there are multiple categories with mixed history — some historical and some newly added with no reference: 

The system will trigger a second LLM callout. 

The prediction will carry a low confidence score and be flagged for manual review. 

Base score 

e. Some GL Categories Have History, None Are New 

If multiple categories have partial historical data but no new categories are introduced: 

The system will perform a second LLM callout for further validation before deciding. 

If single code in GL/CC Prediction Strategy-> 0.5*Si(LLM given desc)+0.2F+0.3R(most recent) 

 
if multiple codes in GL/CC prediction Strategy -> Cs of given category/Sum of all categories 

 

f. All Categories Are Newly Added (No History) 

If every GL Category is new and has no historical reference: 

The system cannot find any matching GL Code. 

The result is “No GL Code Found.” 

0 

 

Cost Centre (CC) Code Détermination Logic 

Once the GL Category (and GL Code) is identified, the Cost Centre is determined using the following rules: 

Priority on Historical Match 

First, check historical data for CC code where the selected GL Code was used with the same vendor and requester combination. 

Fallback Check Within Initial LLM Results 

If no CC Code is found in history for the selected vendor/requester, check among other GL Categories returned in the first LLM callout.  

A low confidence score will be assigned 

No Full Dataset Search 

The system does not re-check the entire historical dataset. 

This is to maintain prediction performance and ensure results remain aligned with the context of the current transaction. 

 
